---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { loadContent } from "../../lib/content";
import { calBookingUrl } from "../../lib/site";

const { provider } = loadContent();
---

<Layout
  title={`Light – Reflection & Refraction | CBSE Class 10 Science | ${provider.name}`}
  description="Complete CBSE Class 10 Science chapter on Light – Reflection & Refraction. Covers laws of reflection, spherical mirrors, refraction, lenses, mirror and lens formulas, and power of a lens."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/subjects/">Subjects</a> / Light – Reflection &amp; Refraction
    </nav>

    <div class="resource-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">CBSE Class 10 · Science · Chapter 10</span>
      <h1>Light – Reflection &amp; Refraction</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A complete one-shot revision of the full chapter: laws of reflection, spherical mirrors,
        image formation, refraction, lenses, formulas and the power of a lens — everything you need
        for your board exams.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Key concepts -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key Concepts at a Glance</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>⚡ Laws of Reflection</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>The angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection.</li>
            <li>The incident ray, the reflected ray and the normal all lie in the same plane.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🪞 Spherical Mirror Terms</h3>
          <dl class="term-list">
            <dt>Pole (P)</dt><dd>Centre of the reflecting surface.</dd>
            <dt>Centre of Curvature (C)</dt><dd>Centre of the sphere of which the mirror is a part.</dd>
            <dt>Radius of Curvature (R)</dt><dd>Distance PC = R = 2f.</dd>
            <dt>Principal Focus (F)</dt><dd>Concave: rays converge here. Convex: rays appear to diverge from here.</dd>
            <dt>Focal Length (f)</dt><dd>Distance PF; f = R/2.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📐 Mirror Formula</h3>
          <p class="formula">1/v + 1/u = 1/f</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>u</strong> – object distance (always −ve for real objects)</li>
            <li><strong>v</strong> – image distance</li>
            <li><strong>f</strong> – focal length (−ve concave, +ve convex)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="formula-sub">Magnification: <strong>m = −v/u</strong></p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🌊 Laws of Refraction (Snell's Law)</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>The incident ray, refracted ray and normal are coplanar.</li>
            <li>n₁ sin θ₁ = n₂ sin θ₂</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Refractive index: <strong>n = c / v</strong> (speed of light in vacuum ÷ speed in medium).</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🔭 Spherical Lens Terms</h3>
          <dl class="term-list">
            <dt>Optical Centre (O)</dt><dd>Rays passing through it emerge undeviated.</dd>
            <dt>Principal Focus (F)</dt><dd>Convex: real focus. Concave: virtual focus.</dd>
            <dt>Focal Length (f)</dt><dd>+ve for convex, −ve for concave.</dd>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📏 Lens Formula &amp; Power</h3>
          <p class="formula">1/v − 1/u = 1/f</p>
          <p class="formula-sub">Magnification: <strong>m = v/u</strong></p>
          <p class="formula-sub">Power: <strong>P = 1/f (metres)</strong>, unit = Dioptre (D)</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Convex lens → +ve power</li>
            <li>Concave lens → −ve power</li>
            <li>Combined lenses: P = P₁ + P₂ + …</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Ray Rules Section -->
    <section class="section" id="ray-rules">
      <div class="rules-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Ray Diagram Fundamentals</span>
        <h2>Visual Rules for Ray Diagrams</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          To construct any image in CBSE board exams, trace <strong>any two</strong> of these standard rays from the top of the object. Learn the rules visually below:
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Tab Switcher -->
      <div class="rules-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Ray rules categories">
        <button class="button rules-tab-btn active" id="tab-btn-mirrors" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-mirrors">
          🪞 Spherical Mirrors (Concave &amp; Convex)
        </button>
        <button class="button secondary rules-tab-btn" id="tab-btn-lenses" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-lenses">
          🔍 Spherical Lenses (Convex &amp; Concave)
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- Mirrors Tab Content -->
      <div class="rules-panel" id="panel-mirrors" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-btn-mirrors">
        <div class="grid two rules-grid">
          <!-- Mirror Rule 1 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 1 · Ray Parallel to Principal Axis</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 1: Ray parallel to axis passes through focus">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="m1-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="m1-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="110" x2="340" y2="110" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="103" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Mirror arc -->
                <path d="M 285 28 Q 306 110 285 192" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="4" fill="none" />
                <!-- Hatching -->
                <path d="M 288 35 l 11 -8 M 294 62 l 11 -8 M 298 90 l 11 -8 M 300 110 l 11 -8 M 298 135 l 11 -8 M 294 160 l 11 -8 M 288 185 l 11 -8" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">C</text>
                <circle cx="205" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="205" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F</text>
                <circle cx="298" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="312" y="114" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">P</text>
                <!-- Incident Ray -->
                <line x1="30" y1="55" x2="165" y2="55" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m1-arr-in)" />
                <line x1="165" y1="55" x2="292" y2="55" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Reflected Ray -->
                <line x1="292" y1="55" x2="185" y2="122" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m1-arr-out)" />
                <line x1="185" y1="122" x2="120" y2="165" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Parallel to Principal Axis → Passes through Focus (F)</h4>
              <p>A ray parallel to the principal axis, after reflection from a concave mirror, <strong>passes through the principal focus (F)</strong>. (In a convex mirror, it appears to diverge from F behind the mirror).</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Reflected Ray</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Mirror Rule 2 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 2 · Ray Passing Through Focus</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 2: Ray through focus emerges parallel to axis">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="m2-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="m2-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="110" x2="340" y2="110" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="103" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Mirror arc -->
                <path d="M 285 28 Q 306 110 285 192" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="4" fill="none" />
                <!-- Hatching -->
                <path d="M 288 35 l 11 -8 M 294 62 l 11 -8 M 298 90 l 11 -8 M 300 110 l 11 -8 M 298 135 l 11 -8 M 294 160 l 11 -8 M 288 185 l 11 -8" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">C</text>
                <circle cx="205" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="205" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F</text>
                <circle cx="298" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="312" y="114" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">P</text>
                <!-- Incident Ray through F -->
                <line x1="120" y1="55" x2="215" y2="116" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m2-arr-in)" />
                <line x1="215" y1="116" x2="292" y2="165" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Reflected Ray parallel -->
                <line x1="292" y1="165" x2="160" y2="165" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m2-arr-out)" />
                <line x1="160" y1="165" x2="30" y2="165" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Through Focus (F) → Emerges Parallel to Principal Axis</h4>
              <p>This is the exact inverse of Rule 1 (principle of reversibility of light). A ray passing through F reflects back <strong>parallel to the principal axis</strong>.</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Reflected Ray</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Mirror Rule 3 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 3 · Ray Through Centre of Curvature</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 3: Ray through C reflects back along same path">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="m3-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="m3-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="110" x2="340" y2="110" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="103" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Mirror arc -->
                <path d="M 285 28 Q 306 110 285 192" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="4" fill="none" />
                <!-- Hatching -->
                <path d="M 288 35 l 11 -8 M 294 62 l 11 -8 M 298 90 l 11 -8 M 300 110 l 11 -8 M 298 135 l 11 -8 M 294 160 l 11 -8 M 288 185 l 11 -8" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">C</text>
                <circle cx="205" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="205" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F</text>
                <circle cx="298" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="312" y="114" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">P</text>
                <!-- Ray through C to mirror (single line retracing) -->
                <line x1="35" y1="87" x2="292" y2="165" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Inward arrow -->
                <line x1="160" y1="125" x2="215" y2="142" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m3-arr-in)" />
                <!-- Outward arrow -->
                <line x1="215" y1="142" x2="160" y2="125" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m3-arr-out)" />
                <!-- Normal indicator -->
                <text x="250" y="185" font-size="10" fill="#a12b2b" font-weight="600">∠i = 0°, ∠r = 0° (Normal incidence)</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Through Centre of Curvature (C) → Retraces Same Path</h4>
              <p>Since the line from C to the mirror surface is a normal (radius), light strikes perpendicularly with <strong>angle of incidence i = 0°</strong>. It reflects straight back along the exact same path.</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Reflected Ray (Retraces)</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Mirror Rule 4 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 4 · Oblique Ray Incident at Pole</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 4: Ray incident at pole reflects at equal angle">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="m4-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="m4-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="110" x2="340" y2="110" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="103" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Mirror arc -->
                <path d="M 285 28 Q 306 110 285 192" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="4" fill="none" />
                <!-- Hatching -->
                <path d="M 288 35 l 11 -8 M 294 62 l 11 -8 M 298 90 l 11 -8 M 300 110 l 11 -8 M 298 135 l 11 -8 M 294 160 l 11 -8 M 288 185 l 11 -8" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="110" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">C</text>
                <circle cx="205" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="205" y="128" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F</text>
                <circle cx="298" cy="110" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="312" y="114" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">P</text>
                <!-- Incident Ray to Pole -->
                <line x1="80" y1="40" x2="195" y2="77" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m4-arr-in)" />
                <line x1="195" y1="77" x2="298" y2="110" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Reflected Ray from Pole -->
                <line x1="298" y1="110" x2="195" y2="143" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#m4-arr-out)" />
                <line x1="195" y1="143" x2="80" y2="180" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Angle Arcs -->
                <path d="M 265 99 A 35 35 0 0 0 263 110" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" />
                <text x="250" y="103" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#b8561c">∠i</text>
                <path d="M 263 110 A 35 35 0 0 0 265 121" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" />
                <text x="250" y="124" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">∠r</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Incident Obliquely at Pole (P) → Follows ∠i = ∠r</h4>
              <p>A ray striking the pole reflects symmetrically about the principal axis such that the <strong>angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection (∠i = ∠r)</strong>.</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Reflected Ray</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Lenses Tab Content -->
      <div class="rules-panel" id="panel-lenses" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-btn-lenses" hidden>
        <div class="grid two rules-grid">
          <!-- Lens Rule 1 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 1 · Ray Parallel to Principal Axis</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 1 for Lenses: Parallel ray passes through F2">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="l1-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="l1-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="105" x2="340" y2="105" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="98" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Convex Lens -->
                <path d="M 180 20 Q 164 105 180 190 Q 196 105 180 20" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" fill="rgba(15, 76, 92, 0.12)" />
                <line x1="180" y1="20" x2="180" y2="190" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="45" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="45" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">2F₁</text>
                <circle cx="110" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F₁</text>
                <circle cx="180" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="180" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">O</text>
                <circle cx="250" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="250" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F₂</text>
                <circle cx="315" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="315" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">2F₂</text>
                <!-- Incident Ray -->
                <line x1="30" y1="55" x2="115" y2="55" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#l1-arr-in)" />
                <line x1="115" y1="55" x2="180" y2="55" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Refracted Ray through F2 -->
                <line x1="180" y1="55" x2="260" y2="112" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#l1-arr-out)" />
                <line x1="260" y1="112" x2="325" y2="158" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Parallel to Principal Axis → Passes through Focus F₂</h4>
              <p>In a convex lens, a ray of light parallel to the principal axis refracts through the lens and <strong>passes through the principal focus (F₂)</strong> on the other side. (In a concave lens, it appears to diverge from F₁).</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Refracted Ray</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Lens Rule 2 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 2 · Ray Through Focus F₁</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 2 for Lenses: Ray through F1 emerges parallel">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="l2-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="l2-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="105" x2="340" y2="105" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="98" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Convex Lens -->
                <path d="M 180 20 Q 164 105 180 190 Q 196 105 180 20" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" fill="rgba(15, 76, 92, 0.12)" />
                <line x1="180" y1="20" x2="180" y2="190" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="45" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="45" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">2F₁</text>
                <circle cx="110" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F₁</text>
                <circle cx="180" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="180" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">O</text>
                <circle cx="250" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="250" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F₂</text>
                <circle cx="315" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="315" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">2F₂</text>
                <!-- Incident Ray through F1 -->
                <line x1="45" y1="55" x2="120" y2="108" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#l2-arr-in)" />
                <line x1="120" y1="108" x2="180" y2="155" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Refracted Ray parallel -->
                <line x1="180" y1="155" x2="260" y2="155" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#l2-arr-out)" />
                <line x1="260" y1="155" x2="330" y2="155" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Through Focus F₁ → Emerges Parallel to Principal Axis</h4>
              <p>A ray passing through the first principal focus (F₁), after refraction from a convex lens, <strong>emerges parallel to the principal axis</strong>.</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Refracted Ray</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Lens Rule 3 -->
          <article class="card rule-card">
            <div class="rule-badge">Rule 3 · Ray Through Optical Centre (O)</div>
            <div class="rule-diagram">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 360 210" class="ray-svg" aria-label="Rule 3 for Lenses: Ray through O passes undeviated">
                <defs>
                  <marker id="l3-arr-in" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#b8561c" />
                  </marker>
                  <marker id="l3-arr-out" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                  </marker>
                </defs>
                <rect width="360" height="210" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" />
                <!-- Principal axis -->
                <line x1="20" y1="105" x2="340" y2="105" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
                <text x="25" y="98" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" font-weight="600">Principal Axis</text>
                <!-- Convex Lens -->
                <path d="M 180 20 Q 164 105 180 190 Q 196 105 180 20" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" fill="rgba(15, 76, 92, 0.12)" />
                <line x1="180" y1="20" x2="180" y2="190" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
                <!-- Points -->
                <circle cx="45" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="45" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">2F₁</text>
                <circle cx="110" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="110" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F₁</text>
                <circle cx="180" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="180" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">O</text>
                <circle cx="250" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="250" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">F₂</text>
                <circle cx="315" cy="105" r="3.5" fill="#0f4c5c" />
                <text x="315" y="123" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f4c5c">2F₂</text>
                <!-- Straight ray through O without deviation -->
                <line x1="35" y1="45" x2="120" y2="80" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#l3-arr-in)" />
                <line x1="120" y1="80" x2="180" y2="105" stroke="#b8561c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <line x1="180" y1="105" x2="255" y2="136" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#l3-arr-out)" />
                <line x1="255" y1="136" x2="325" y2="165" stroke="#0f4c5c" stroke-width="2.5" />
                <!-- Callout -->
                <text x="180" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#0f4c5c" font-weight="bold">No deviation at O</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-body">
              <h4>Through Optical Centre (O) → Goes Undeviated</h4>
              <p>A ray of light passing through the optical centre (O) of a thin lens <strong>passes without suffering any deviation or bending</strong>. This is the simplest ray to draw in exam diagrams!</p>
              <div class="rule-legend">
                <span class="legend-tag inc"><span class="dot inc"></span> Incident Ray</span>
                <span class="legend-tag ref"><span class="dot ref"></span> Emerging Ray (Straight)</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Image formation summary -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Image Formation — Quick Reference</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap card">
